"The coefficient-shape conjecture for P_k(t,x) — MathDB (https://mathdb.com/p/334352/the-coefficient-shape-conjecture-for-p-k-t-x)\nciteturn2search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; The coefficient-shape conjecture for $P_k(t,x)$P k​(t,x) ... Svinin, “Conjectures involving a generalization of the sums of powers of integers”, arXiv:1610.05387 (2017).\n\nThe coefficient-shape conjecture for $P_k(t,x)$P k​(t,x)\n\nConjecture open\n\nWrite\n\n$$P_k(t,x)=x\\left(p_{k,0}(t)x^{k-1}-p_{k,1}(t)x^{k-2}+\\cdots+(-1)^{k-1}p_{k,k-1}(t)\\right).$$P k​(t,x)=x(p k,0​(t)x k−1−p k,1​(t)x k−2+⋯+(−1)k−1 p k,k−1​(t)).\n\nThus $p_{k,j}(t)$p k,j​(t) denotes the coefficient functions in this expansion. Coefficient-shape conjecture. The coefficients satisfy\n\n$$p_{k,j}(t)=\\frac{r_{k,j}(t)}{t^j},$$p k,j​(t)=t j r k,j​(t)​,\n\nwhere\n\n$$r_{k,j}(t)=\\sum_{q=0}^{m}\\alpha_{k,j,q}t^{2q}(t+1)^{j-3q},$$r k,j​(t)=q=0∑m​α k,j,q​t 2 q(t+1)j−3 q,\n\nwith rational positive nonzero numbers $\\alpha_{k,j,q}$α k,j,q​; here $m\\geq 0$m≥0 and $j=3m+l$j=3 m+l for some remainder $l$l on division of $j$j by $3$3. The claim is based on calculations of the displayed polynomials $P_k(t,x)$P k​(t,x); no proof or resolution is given in the source.\n\n## Progress summary\n\nRefresh\n\nNothing recorded yet. Refresh searches the literature and the public web for attempts on this problem, and writes the first summary here.\n\nsource: Andrei K. Svinin, “Conjectures involving a generalization of the sums of powers of integers”, arXiv:1610.05387 (2017).\n\ncombinatoricsnumber-theorypolynomial-sequences\n\n0\n\nposted by arXiv 2 days ago\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nau:Svinin_A in:math - SciRate Search (https://scirate.com/search?q=au%3ASvinin_A+in%3Amath)\nciteturn2search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; Oct 19 2016 math.CO math.NT arXiv:1610.05387v2\nOct 16 2017 math.NT arXiv:1710.04779v1\n\n[Button: Scited][Button: Scite!]\n\n0\n\n@misc{1710.04779, author = {Andrei K.~Svinin and Svetlana V.~Svinina}, title = {{B}ernoulli numbers and sums of powers of integers of higher order}, year = {2017}, eprint = {1710.04779}, note = {arXiv:1710.04779v1} }[Button: Copy Citation]\n\nPDF\n\nWe give an expression of polynomials for higher sums of powers of integers via the higher order Bernoulli numbers.\n\n  * Conjectures involving a generalization of the sums of powers of integers\n\nAndrei K. Svinin\n\nOct 19 2016 math.CO math.NT arXiv:1610.05387v2\n\n[Button: Scited][Button: Scite!]\n\n2\n\n@misc{1610.05387, author = {Andrei K.~Svinin}, title = {{C}onjectures involving a generalization of the sums of powers of integers}, year = {2016}, eprint = {1610.05387}, note = {arXiv:1610.05387v2} }[Button: Copy Citation]\n\nPDF\n\nSome class of sums which naturally include the sums of powers of integers is considered. A number of conjectures concerning a representation of these sums is made.\n\n  * Tuenter polynomials and a Catalan triangle\n\nAndrei K. Svinin\n\nMar 21 2016 math.CO arXiv:1603.05748v2\n\n[Button: Scited][Button: Scite!]\n\n0\n\n@misc{1603.05748, author = {Andrei K.~Svinin}, title = {{T}uenter polynomials and a {C}atalan triangle}, year = {2016}, eprint = {1603.05748}, note = {arXiv:1603.05748v2} }[Button: Copy Citation]\n\nPDF\n\nWe consider Tuenter polynomials as linear combinations of descending factorials and show that coefficients of these linear combinations are expressed via a Catalan triangle of numbers. We also describe a triangle of coefficients in terms of some polynomials.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA001840 - OEIS (https://oeis.org/A001840)\nciteturn2search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 7 months ago; Svinin, On some class of sums, arXiv:1610.05387 [math.CO], 2016.\nAndrei K. Svinin, On some class of sums, arXiv:1610.05387 [math.CO], 2016. See p. 7.\n\nEric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, Anarboricity.\n\nEric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, Com