%t Table[(2^(n-1)-1)/n,{n,Prime[Range[2,20]]}] (* _Harvey P. Dale_, Nov 07 2016 *) `\n\n`%o (PARI) `\n\n`%o forprime(p=3, 100, print1((2^(p-1)-1)/p \", \")) \\\\ _Satish Bysany_, Mar 11 2017 `\n\n`%Y Cf. A002322, A001917, A096060, A001045. `\n\n`%K nonn,easy,nice `\n\n`%O 2,2 `\n\n`%A _N. J. A. Sloane_, Sep 19 1994 `--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nau:Berman_L in:math - SciRate Search (https://scirate.com/search?q=au%3ABerman_L+in%3Amath)\nciteturn2search11 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 months ago; Jul 18 2017 math.CO arXiv:1707.05294v2 ... @misc{1707.05294, author = {Leah Wrenn Berman and Déborah Oliveros and Gordon I.\nWilliams】\n\nJul 18 2017 math.CO arXiv:1707.05294v2\n\n[Button: Scited][Button: Scite!]\n\n0\n\n@misc{1707.05294, author = {Leah Wrenn Berman and Déborah Oliveros and Gordon I.~Williams}, title = {{C}yclic pseudo-{L}oupekine snarks}, year = {2017}, eprint = {1707.05294}, note = {arXiv:1707.05294v2} }[Button: Copy Citation]\n\nPDF\n\nIn 1976, Loupekine introduced (via Isaacs) a very general way of constructing new snarks from old snarks by cyclically connecting multipoles constructed from smaller snarks. In this paper, we generalize Loupekine's construction to produce a variety of snarks which can be drawn with $m$-fold rotational symmetry for $m\\geq 3$ (and often, $m$ odd), constructed as $\\mathbb{Z}_{m}$ lifts of \\emphvoltage graphs with certain properties; we call these snarks \\emphcyclic pseudo-Loupekine snarks. In particular, we discuss three infinite families of snarks which can be drawn with $\\mathbb{Z}_{m}$ rotational symmetry whose smallest element is constructed from 3 snarks with 3-fold rotational symmetry on 28 vertices; one family has the property that the oddness of the family increases with $m$. We also develop a new infinite family of snarks, of order $12m$ for each odd $m\\geq 3$, which can be drawn with $m$-fold rotational symmetry and which are constructed beginning with a 3-edge-colorable graph, instead of a snark.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nStructure of Flow-continuous Mappings in Algebraic Context (https://dspace.cuni.cz/bitstream/handle/20.500.11956/173980/140100592.pdf?isAllowed=y&sequence=1)\nciteturn2search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4.8 years ago; Cyclic pseudo-Loupekine snarks, 2017. https://arxiv.org/abs/1707.05294. ... *Graph theory*, volume 173 of *Graduate Texts in Mathematics*.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLoupekine snark (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loupekine_snark)\nciteturn2search13 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 9 months ago; (2014), \"Fulkerson's conjecture and Loupekine snarks\", Discrete Mathematics, 326: 20–28, doi:10.1016/j.disc.2014.02.016, MR 3188983 ... (2024), \"Rotationally symmetric snarks from voltage graphs\", Discrete Mathematics, 347 (4): Paper No. 113874, 15, doi:10.1016/j.disc.2024.113874, MR 4694305; previously announced as \"Cyclic pseudo-Loupekine snarks\", arXiv:1707.05294\n"
